Antigravity's PreToolUse leg (tool-call-stash.ts, advisor.ts, static-plan.ts) and PostToolUse leg (post-tool-use.ts) share stash.ts's on-disk key format (conversationId:stepIdx for the tool-call join, conversationId alone for the pending-injection queue) and run-command.ts's run_command args narrowing (advisor, planner, and touch join must decode the same host shape), none of it type-enforced across files. advisor.ts and post-tool-use.ts both feed appendPendingInjection, which only post-invocation.ts drains, and stop.ts retires the same call-scoped state stash.ts defines; a key-format or lifecycle change on either leg silently orphans the other's writes or reads.
